Hi,

I think that polypiling is no longer as abusive as it used to be in
earlier versions. However, I do think that polypiling spellbooks is still
too powerful.

I suggest that spellbooks have a 30% chance to keep the same level, then a
30% chance to go down one level, then a 30% chance to go down two levels,
... until the level of the book is reached.

If the chance to become level 1 is missed, it would become a blank
spellbook (keeping its charges though: the number of charges should still
go down by one with every polymorph).

This would prevent players from gathering, say, 5 spellbooks, and learning
almost all spells with those few. Especially, it would make learning the
higher level spells rarer.

